lesson coding-when-the-flag-is-tapped v=1 format=teach grade=1 unit=6 subject=coding levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "When the flag is tapped"
  goal "Read a program that starts when the flag is tapped, and say where the rabbit ends up."

  look {
    scene 34x10 {
      row all at=canvas(1, 0) space=1 align=start {
        blocks b code=["when the flag is tapped", "right 3", "jump", "say hello"]
        stage s cols=7 col=1 who=rabbit code=["when the flag is tapped", "right 3", "jump", "say hello"]
      }
    }
    say """
      The yellow block on top says when the program starts. Nothing happens until the flag is
      tapped, and then the blocks under it run from the top. On the screen, tap the flag on the
      stage.
      """
  }
  do {
    practice coding.stage-where count=2 seed=3
    show coding.stage-nothing-yet s=2 a=3 t=0 easy-s=1 easy-a=2 hard-s=3 hard-a=4
    show coding.stage-nothing-yet s=1 a=4 t=1 easy-a=2 hard-s=3
    practice coding.stage-crab-left count=2 seed=4
    practice coding.stage-start-square count=2 seed=5
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show coding.stage-flag-twice s=1 a=3 easy-a=2
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show coding.stage-fewest-blocks e=8 easy-e=5 hard-e=9
  }
  remember {
    say "A when block starts the program. The blocks under it run in order."
  }

  grown-ups """
    A when block is the start of a program rather than a step in it, which is the idea of an event.
    If the child wants to, let them choose what the rabbit does after the jump and act it out.
    Two questions ask where the rabbit is before and after the flag is tapped, which is the whole
    idea: until the flag is tapped, nothing moves. In the two-star question the flag is tapped twice,
    and the second run starts from where the first one stopped. In the three-star question it helps
    to use as many right 3 blocks as will fit and see what is left.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the rabbit moves two squares at a time from the first square, so every answer can be counted along the stage."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the crab goes left four and back three, the rabbit starts further along, and the fewest blocks have to reach square nine."
  }
}
